  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1, vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1921 Edward B. Marks sheet music (page images from the Library of Congress public image service and the LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b9/scan/), key B flat major, 6/8 (durations in quarter-note beats), starting on the 3-eighth pickup. Simplifications (chromatic notes played as the nearest drum note): the two C sharps (chromatic passing notes on 'Let it re-SOUND' and 'Let us MARCH') are played as 2 (C); the four G flats in 'Sing a song full of the hope that the present has brought us' (a borrowed minor 6th, b6) are played as 6 (G), which loses the line's darker colour. Range low 3 to 6. D drum: the notes as written. C drum (no low 3 or low 4): the two 'Sing a song full of...' lines, up to the first note of 'brought', are played an octave higher, so the octave leap on 'brought' becomes a repeated note. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
